{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.archimedean_braid_structure","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.archimedean_braid_structure","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.SpecificGroups.Quaternion"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.descartes_braid_structure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.descartes_braid_structure","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/archimedean_braid_structure.lean#L32-L53","doc":"**Descartes braid structure** (claims i–ii).\n\nLet `(C, A, τ)` be a Descartes universe.  The braiding of\n`C = Rep(SU_q(2))` induces a representation\n`ρ₃ : B₃ → Aut_C(V⊗³)` whose image in `SU(2)` (via the fibre functor `τ`)\nis the binary dihedral group `Dic₃` of order `12`\n([manuscript claims (i) faithful image of order ≥ 12, (ii) image is\n`Dic₃` of order `12`]).\n\nThe single conjectural input is the **group isomorphism**\n`himg : G ≃* Dic₃` identifying the braid image `G` with `Dic₃` — the open\ncategorical fact.  Both numerical claims are then *derived*: the order is\n`12` by transport along `himg` and `dic3_card`, and faithfulness\n(`order ≥ 12`) follows.  (Claims (iii) three `S₃` colour-sectors and\n(iv) `p`-adic universality concern the ambient `S₅` and base ring and are\ntracked separately.) ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:cor:descartes-braid-structure","label":"cor:descartes-braid-structure","md":"quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-braid-structure.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.dic3_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.dic3_card","kind":"theorem","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/archimedean_braid_structure.lean#L24-L30","doc":"`Dic₃` has order `12` — a genuine computation via\n`QuaternionGroup.card` (`4 * 3 = 12`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.Dic3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.Dic3","kind":"def","line":19,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/archimedean_braid_structure.lean#L19-L22","doc":"The binary dihedral (dicyclic) group `Dic₃` — the image of `ρ₃` in\n`SU(2)`.  Concretely Mathlib's `QuaternionGroup 3` (the generalised\nquaternion / dicyclic group of order `4·3 = 12`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}